## Goal
A failed retained macro product must not poison a fresh or edited unrelated requested root. Failed demand remains owned and repairable, but is not permission to run or report unrelated compiler work.

## Evidence and attribution
During cold review of fz-tfn.46, the real regression below failed: after main's macro fails lowering Missing.value(), fresh healthy()=7 returns an error from RootBackendProduct(root3), not 7. Log /tmp/fz-tfn46-healthy-macro.log. ProductSessions::next_request drains requested/pending_requests globally; ExecutionContext::drive_product_requests unconditionally requeues and returns the first failed address. The same retry_request/next_request/drain logic is present at ad0ac47d3; tfn.46 changes only the boxed error representation at that boundary. This is source-level predecessor attribution, NOT a claimed executable baseline reproduction. Establish the smallest executable predecessor proof before repair.

## Scope and ordering
Independent existing product-demand ownership defect found during failure-read ownership review; put at the epic tail under the user's new-issue rule, blocking fz-tfn.39 final cleanup. It does not authorize weakening tfn.46's exact failed job reads, diagnostics, source repair or claim withdrawal. No global scheduling changes are to be silently included in tfn.46. If evidence shows these changes cannot land atomically apart, revise dependency ordering and resolve the blocker first.

## Strategy and acceptance
- Read .agent/strategies/output-contract-loop.md; trace exact requested root/product/subscriber ownership before editing.
- Preserve one World fact authority and one retained ProductMemo authority. Collapse redundant demand/queue authority if justified. No swallowed diagnostics, dropped standing demand, private root cones, global rescans, unconditional retries or display-string identity.
- Preserve the failed root's original diagnostics and exact relevant repair; unchanged failed demand must do no producer work.
- Pin failed macro then fresh healthy7, unchanged healthy7, edited healthy8, and failed root still errors. Also pin subsequent macro source repair and nested active roots/shared products.
- Causal counts prove no unrelated failure work. Required interp/native/AOT, artifact determinism, full library, serial fixture matrix, CLI, strict lint/fmt/docs gates and cold ticket-scoped review before separate commit/close.
- Remove temporary baseline probes; integrate regression into appropriate existing tests rather than leave duplicate compiles.

## Preserved regression (test body; use existing macro_product_test imports)
```rust
#[test]
fn failed_macro_product_does_not_poison_a_fresh_unrelated_root() {
    let mut compiler = Compiler2::new(ConfiguredTelemetry::new());
    compiler.submit_code(CodeSubmission {
        name: Some("unrelated_failed_macro.fz".into()),
        text: "defmacro answer() do\n quote do: unquote(Missing.value())\nend\nfn main(), do: answer()\n".into(),
    });
    let failed = compiler.submit_root(RootSubmission {
        module_name: None,
        name: "main".into(),
        arity: 0,
        need: ExecutableNeed::Value,
    });
    assert!(compiler.run_root_interp(failed).is_err());
    compiler.submit_code(CodeSubmission {
        name: Some("fresh_healthy_root.fz".into()),
        text: "fn healthy(), do: 7\n".into(),
    });
    let healthy = compiler.submit_root(RootSubmission {
        module_name: None,
        name: "healthy".into(),
        arity: 0,
        need: ExecutableNeed::Value,
    });
    assert_eq!(compiler.run_root_interp(healthy), Ok(7));
    compiler.submit_code(CodeSubmission {
        name: Some("edited_healthy_root.fz".into()),
        text: "fn healthy(), do: 8\n".into(),
    });
    assert_eq!(compiler.run_root_interp(healthy), Ok(8));
    assert!(compiler.run_root_interp(failed).is_err());
}
```
